    "lawCode": "Amd §§4, 5, 6 & 21, Chap 416 of 2007",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7157A\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 416 of the laws of 2007, establishing the city\nof Rochester and the board of education of the city school district of\nthe city of Rochester school facilities modernization program act, in\nrelation to granting further authority to the RJSCB to modernize educa-\ntional facilities in the city of Rochester\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize a 12 project, $600 million phase III Rochester Joint\nSchools Construction Board School Modernization Program (RJSCB)\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 outlines the project authorization, the comprehensive school\nfacilities modernization plan, and project selection featured in\nsections 4, 5 and 6 of chapter 416 laws from 2007\n\nSection 2 of the bill authorizes another twelve (12) projects in Phase\nIII up to a total cost of $600 million. This section also: further\ndelineates the process for extending, rebidding, and entering contracts;\nthe process for selecting projects; and requires a report to be submit-\nted on phase III on or before June 30, 2033.\n\nSection 3 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIt has long been recognized that a healthy and welcoming learning envi-\nronment promotes greater educational attainment. Passage of this legis-\nlation will allow for a seamless transition from Phase II to Phase III\nto prevent disruption of the academic process and unnecessary costs.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nPhase I of this Program was authorized through Chapter 416 of the Laws\nof 2007. Phase II was authorized through Chapter 533 of the laws of\n2014, and through Chapter 92 of the Laws of 2016 signed by the Governor\nof the State of New York on July 5, 2016. Phase III of this program was\nauthorized through Chapter 614 of the laws of 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTotal cost to the State and Local government to be determined. This\nlegislation authorizes construction up to $600 million for the proposed\nPhase III Strategic Plan.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
